From dac1ac9ce08aa610e6f2aa7eef1e4e99130c196a
Subject: wasm_threaded_loader: cancel in-flight loads through the task
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/dac1ac9ce08aa610e6f2aa7eef1e4e99130c196a
Date: 2026-10-30T12:40:11Z

With web tasks cancelling on drop, the web keeps its load tasks in
`pending_tasks` like native does (only a single-threaded pool detaches),
so dropping an asset's last strong handle aborts the main-thread load.
The worker answers each request over a oneshot and races the load
against the sender's cancellation, which resolves when that task is
gone; the work future drops with it, and the fetch and its request slot
go too.

This replaces the 2 s `path_to_id` poll from ede652c2a: gloo-timers, the
`LoadCancelled` variant and the widened `path_to_id` visibility are
reverted.
